# Format & Lint (Agent workflow)

When you **create or substantially edit** files in this repo:

## 1. Prettier — immediately after writing

Format every new or changed file right after it is written:

```bash
pnpm exec prettier --write <path>…
```

- Pass **explicit paths** (created/edited files), not the whole repo, unless many files changed.
- Applies to source, config, and markdown files Prettier supports in this project.
- **`docs/decisions.md`** — always include when updating ADRs (table rows are easy to miss).

## Pre-commit (husky + lint-staged)

Staged files are auto-formatted and ESLint-fixed on `git commit` via `.husky/pre-commit`. This catches forgotten Prettier runs before CI; agents should still format touched paths immediately after writing.

## 2. ESLint — before marking the task done

Run a short lint check on the same touched paths:

```bash
pnpm exec eslint <path>…
```

- Fix auto-fixable issues in the same edit batch.
- Resolve remaining errors; do not leave new lint failures from your changes.

## When to skip

- Read-only tasks (reviews, explanations, questions).
- Changes limited to files outside Prettier/ESLint scope (e.g. binary assets).
